  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_lamprey_cb14ca03ce2a398754cdda35d7ca3a822e8b8790a637d1d0cdc9f12cedc30fdc4e4">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>lamprey | lampreys | an edible fish of the genus Petromyzon, resembling an eel in shape and in having no scales. It has a mouth like a sucker, pouch-like gills, seven spiracles or apertures on each side of the head, and a fistula or opening on the top of the head (OED s.v. lamprey)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
